Squid configuration writes
==========================

The packaged squidstats.service intentionally runs as the unprivileged
``squidstats`` account with ``ProtectSystem=full``.  In particular, it does
not have a writable exception for /etc/squid, which may contain Kerberos
keytabs and other credentials.

The Kerberos administration page is consequently manual-only in the Debian
package.  It may generate a validated preview, but it will not write
squid.conf or keytabs.  Apply the preview through the site's controlled
administrative configuration procedure and validate it with Squid before
reloading the service.

Do not make /etc/squid broadly writable and do not grant the web process
access to keytabs.  A deployment that needs managed writes must first provide
a separate, narrowly scoped and audited privileged mechanism.  Only then may
it explicitly set SQUIDSTATS_SQUID_CONFIG_WRITE_MODE=managed in a systemd
drop-in; that setting changes the application contract, but grants no
filesystem permission by itself.
